.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-297-
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-298-## 4. Protocol
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-299-
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-300-1. **Build the spike** — a throwaway renderer over existing `buildModuleGraph`
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-301-   output. No IR design, no schema, no viewer polish, no new CLI command. It may
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-302-   be ugly. It may be deleted afterwards.
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-303-2. **Separate the builder from the answerer.** Whoever renders the map must not
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-304-   be whoever answers the questions. Under whyline roles that is natural: the
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log:305:   implementer renders, the reviewer answers cold.
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-306-3. **Counterbalance the order.** Answer Q1 and Q3 from the Markdown first, Q2
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-307-   and Q4 from the map first. Answering the same question twice in a fixed order
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-308-   measures memory, not the artifact.
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-309-4. **Record per question:** the answer given, whether it was correct, roughly
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-310-   how long it took, and stated confidence *before* the answer is checked.
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-311-5. **Correctness is judged against the graph**, not against the answerer's
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-312-   impression. `sonde query` is the adjudicator.
.whyline/relay/logs/MAP-GATE-1-3-codex-review.log-313-
--
